[0.501, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿ 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 429 429\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿ HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿ X-RateLimit-Limit: 10\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.701, "o", "Rate limiting is now on all `/api` routes, backed by your Upstash database\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "`mcpeval-ratelimit-e18kih`. I ran the server and sent 12 requests in a row: the first 10 got\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "`200` and the last 2 got `429 Too Many Requests` with `Retry-After: 10`.\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.091, "o", "**What changed**\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "- **`server.js`**: added middleware using `@upstash/ratelimit`. Each client IP gets 10 requests\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "per 10 seconds, counted over a rolling window. Every response includes `X-RateLimit-Limit`,\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "`X-RateLimit-Remaining` and `X-RateLimit-Reset` headers. Blocked requests get a 429 plus a\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "`Retry-After` header. If Redis can't be reached, requests are let through and the error is\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "logged, so a Redis outage doesn't take the API down.\r\n"]
[0.091, "o", "- **`package.json`**: added `@upstash/ratelimit` and `@upstash/redis`. `npm start` now runs\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "`node --env-file=.env server.js`, which loads the credentials from `.env`.\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "- **`.env`**: holds the database's REST URL and token, which I fetched from Upstash. It is\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "gitignored. `.env.example` lists the variable names with no values.\r\n"]
[0.091, "o", "- **`.gitignore`**: ignores `node_modules/` and `.env`.\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "**Before you deploy**\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "- **Proxies:** if the app runs behind a proxy or load balancer, add `app.set(\"trust proxy\", 1)`.\r\n"]
[0.090, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[1mPASS\u001b[0m \u001b[2m(checked through the upstash CLI, 38s)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m depends on @upstash/ratelimit\r\n  \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m depends on @upstash/redis\r\n  \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m server code uses Ratelimit\r\n  \u001b[32m✓\u001b[0m env points at the DB"]
